🔴🟡🟢 Week 1 — C
Transition from visual to text-based programming with C. You learn how a computer actually executes code — no magic.

Key Concepts
•	Source code vs. machine code — humans write source; computers run machine code
•	Compiling with clang / make — converting source to executable
•	Variables and data types: int, float, char, string, bool
•	Operators: +, -, *, /, % (modulo)
•	Conditionals: if, else if, else, switch
•	Loops: for, while, do-while
•	Functions — named blocks of code you can call and reuse
•	Command-line interface (CLI) basics
•	printf and scanf — output and input in C
•	cs50.h library: get_int(), get_string(), get_float()

 project Scratch project 
